id: SceneFilenameManager
name: ᝯㄝₓ Scene Filename Manager
metadata:
  description: "A file's name is metadata nothing else in Stash remembers: once a file is renamed, by hand or by another tool, the name it had is gone. This plugin keeps a copy of every scene's filename in a custom field, and can put it back.\n\nArchive Original Filenames, in Settings → Tasks, writes the name of each scene's primary file, without its extension, into the custom field named below, on every scene that does not carry that field yet. A scene that already carries it is never overwritten, so the field keeps the first name the plugin saw; delete the field on a scene and the next run archives it again under its current name.\n\nRestore Original Filenames renames the primary file of every scene back to the archived name, keeping the file's current extension and its folder, wherever the two differ. A scene whose archived name could not be a filename is listed as skipped rather than renamed, and a name already taken in the folder fails for that scene alone.\n\nBoth tasks list every scene they would touch before anything is written, write nothing until you press Proceed, and Undo reverses what the dialog wrote while it stays open. With ᝯㄝₓ Custom Fields Bulk Editor installed, the field is given a description there.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer: a scene's custom fields are where the name is kept."
version: 0.1.0
